    {
      "title": "Two three-carbon feedstocks",
      "stem": "The figure shows two candidate feedstocks for making a cable coating. In a separate fuel test, 0.100 mol of the saturated feedstock is burned completely. Use M(CO₂)=44.0 g mol⁻¹.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Identify which feedstock undergoes addition polymerization and draw two consecutive repeat units using a condensed formula with continuation bonds.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Give a chemical test distinguishing the two feedstocks. Include the observation for each and state a condition that prevents confusion with a substitution reaction.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Write the complete combustion equation for the saturated feedstock and find the mass of CO₂ released in the fuel test.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "d",
          "prompt": "Explain why the polymer can insulate a wire while the metal core conducts.",
          "marks": 2
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Propene contains C=C and can undergo addition polymerization."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Two repeats: –CH₂–CH(CH₃)–CH₂–CH(CH₃)– with continuation bonds."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "The backbone bonds are single and the methyl branches are attached to alternating backbone carbons."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Use bromine water without UV illumination."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Propene decolourizes it by addition across C=C."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Propane shows no rapid decolourization under these conditions; avoid UV initiation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "C₃H₈+5O₂→3CO₂+4H₂O."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "0.300 mol CO₂ corresponds to 13.2 g."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "The covalent polymer lacks mobile ions or delocalized electrons available to move through it."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "The metal contains mobile delocalized electrons, so the two materials have different electrical roles."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
