    {
      "title": "An energy estimate for a fuel cell reactant",
      "stem": "Consider the combustion H₂(g)+½O₂(g)→H₂O(g). Mean bond enthalpies in kJ mol⁻¹ are H–H 436, O=O 498 and O–H 463. The enthalpy of condensation of water at the reference temperature is −44.0 kJ mol⁻¹.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Use the bond data to estimate the combustion enthalpy to gaseous water.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Calculate the enthalpy to liquid water. Explain why specifying the product state matters.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "A device converts 55.0% of the estimated energy for liquid-water formation into useful electrical output. Find the output for 4.00 g H₂. Use M(H₂)=2.016 g mol⁻¹.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "d",
          "prompt": "Give one limitation of the bond-enthalpy estimate and one reason why the point-of-use CO₂ emission alone cannot establish the fuel’s total carbon footprint.",
          "marks": 2
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Breaking reactant bonds requires 436+½(498)=685 kJ mol⁻¹."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Forming two O–H bonds releases 2×463=926 kJ mol⁻¹."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "ΔH≈685−926=−241 kJ mol⁻¹."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Add condensation: −241−44=−285 kJ mol⁻¹."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Further heat is released when intermolecular attractions form in the liquid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Amount=4.00/2.016=1.984 mol."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Estimated chemical energy=1.984×285=565 kJ."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Useful electrical energy≈311 kJ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Mean bond enthalpies are averages over gaseous compounds; actual bond energies may differ."
            },
            {
              "code": "B1",
              "text": "Hydrogen production, compression or transport can consume fossil energy, which must be included in a life-cycle comparison."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "marks": 10,
      "questionType": "structured",
      "answerSummary": "Hydrogen production, compression or transport can consume fossil energy, which must be included in a life-cycle comparison.",
